{
  "name": "How to Plan for Future Mobility Needs in Your Home Remodel?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When you're thinking about remodeling your home, it’s a perfect opportunity to consider future mobility needs. Many homeowners ask how they can make changes now that will support potential future mobility challenges, and how to blend safety with a normal, comfortable design. The key is smart, forward-thinking planning.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2",
      "text": "Start with a room-by-room assessment. Think about where you spend the most time and what areas might become difficult to navigate. Bathrooms and kitchens are usually top priorities, but don't forget about doorways and circulation paths. A good plan will prioritize changes that are disruptive or expensive to add later, like widening doorways or reconfiguring a bathroom layout. Important design considerations include things like curbless showers, which are a game-changer for accessibility, and grab bars that don't scream",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    }
  ],
